/// \defgroup grp_w2_map_file_paths Map folder file names
/// \ingroup grp_common_services
/// \brief Twelve small string functions: four split a path into folder,
///        file name, base name and extension, and eight derive the name of
///        each side file that a map's folder may hold from the path of its
///        `.map` file.
///
/// A map is a folder holding the `.map` file and, optionally, side files
/// next to it: a per-map INI override (`map.ini`), a second INI override
/// (`solo.ini`), a string file, three preview images, a readme and an
/// asset-usage list. These functions only build names. None of them opens
/// a file, checks that one exists or touches the file system, and they
/// take and return AsciiString by value.
/// For a map at `Maps\MyMap\MyMap.map` they return:
///
/// | Function | Result |
/// |---|---|
/// | GetBasePathFromPath | `Maps\MyMap` |
/// | GetFileFromPath | `MyMap.map` |
/// | GetBaseFileFromFile, given `MyMap.map` | `MyMap` |
/// | GetExtensionFromFile, given `MyMap.map` | `map` |
/// | GetPreviewFromMap | `Maps\MyMap\MyMap.tga` |
/// | GetArtPreviewFromMap | `Maps\MyMap\MyMap_art.tga` |
/// | GetPicPreviewFromMap | `Maps\MyMap\MyMap_pic.tga` |
/// | GetINIFromMap | `Maps\MyMap\map.ini` |
/// | GetSoloINIFromMap | `Maps\MyMap\solo.ini` |
/// | GetStrFileFromMap | `Maps\MyMap\map.str` |
/// | GetReadmeFromMap | `Maps\MyMap\readme.txt` |
/// | GetAssetUsageFromMap | `Maps\MyMap\assetusage.txt` |
///
/// \par Who uses them
/// The names serve the multiplayer map transfer, which sends a map to
/// players who do not have it:
/// - GameInfo::setMap stores the game's map name. When the GameInfo's
///   in-game flag is set (Zero Hour: set on entering a game's setup,
///   cleared on leaving it or when the game ends) and this machine is the
///   host, and TheMapCache knows the map, it also builds the map-contents
///   mask, one bit per side file found: it opens each candidate name through
///   TheFileSystem and closes it again. It takes six of the names from
///   GetStrFileFromMap, GetSoloINIFromMap, GetAssetUsageFromMap,
///   GetReadmeFromMap, GetArtPreviewFromMap and GetPicPreviewFromMap. Like
///   Zero Hour's version, it builds the plain preview and `map.ini` names
///   itself. The bits are 1 for a known map, 2 for the preview, 4 for
///   `map.ini`, 8 for `map.str`, 16 for `solo.ini`, 32 for the asset-usage
///   list, 64 for the readme, 128 for the art preview and 256 for the
///   picture preview. Bit 512 is set from two flags of the map's cache
///   entry whose meaning is not established. When the host's TheMapCache
///   does not know the map, setMap clears the mask to 0 instead.
/// - The map-transfer routine runs when a game starts. LANAPI::OnGameStart
///   and GameSpyStagingRoom::launchGame call it, as do their Living World
///   battle counterparts, and then refresh TheMapCache. Zero Hour and
///   BFME 1 call it DoAnyMapTransfers. BFME 2's routine is not described
///   here beyond its calls: its retail code calls GetPreviewFromMap,
///   GetINIFromMap, GetStrFileFromMap, GetSoloINIFromMap,
///   GetAssetUsageFromMap, GetReadmeFromMap, GetArtPreviewFromMap and
///   GetPicPreviewFromMap, in that order. BFME 1: when a human player in
///   slots 1 to 7 lacks the map, the routine sends each side file whose
///   mask bit is set, in that order, then the `.map` file itself, to those
///   players. A set 512 bit then makes it fail before sending anything.
///
/// GetExtensionFromFile has no known direct caller in retail code. Zero
/// Hour defines it without calling it as well.
///
/// \par Zero Hour and BFME 1
/// Zero Hour keeps ten of these functions, with the map-transfer routine,
/// in GameNetwork/FileTransfer.cpp. GetArtPreviewFromMap and
/// GetPicPreviewFromMap are not in Zero Hour. BFME 1 has all twelve.
///
/// \par Modding
/// - The side-file names are fixed in code. `map.ini`, `solo.ini`,
///   `map.str`, `readme.txt` and `assetusage.txt` keep the same names in
///   every map folder. The three previews take the base name of the `.map`
///   file, not of the folder. Renaming the `.map` file means renaming
///   `MyMap.tga`, `MyMap_art.tga` and `MyMap_pic.tga` with it.
/// - No helper here and no contents-mask bit names any other file in the
///   folder, such as `ambientlightmap.tga`, which the game reads when the
///   map loads (\ref sub_gamelogic_map). BFME 1's transfer routine sends
///   only these side files and the `.map` file, so such files likely do
///   not reach a player who receives the map. BFME 2's own routine is
///   known here only by the helpers it calls, so this is likely rather
///   than certain.
/// - What each file does is decided elsewhere. The map loader reads
///   `map.ini` and `solo.ini` as INI overrides and `map.str` as the map's
///   strings (\ref page_modding_ini). Unlike Zero Hour's, it does not
///   read `assetusage.txt` (see GetAssetUsageFromMap).
///   getMapPreviewImage prefers `MyMap_art.tga` to `MyMap.tga` when
///   building the preview it shows.
///   W3DRadar::buildTerrainTexture also looks for an `_art.tga` file,
///   apparently the current map's, and when one exists uses it for the
///   radar instead of drawing the radar image from the terrain. Both build
///   those names themselves rather than calling these helpers.
/// - Folders are separated by backslashes only. A path written with
///   forward slashes has no folder part as far as these functions can see.
///
/// \par Remastering
/// - Windows path rules are built in: only `\` separates folders, and
///   every derived name is formatted with a `\`. A port to a file system
///   that uses `/` can either translate `\` in its file layer, leaving
///   these helpers unchanged, or, if map paths reach them written with
///   `/`, change these helpers and the other code that splits map paths
///   on `\`. That code includes GameInfo::setMap's own `map.ini` lookup,
///   which stops collecting folders once no backslash remains in the
///   path, and getMapPreviewImage, which takes the file name from after
///   the last backslash.
/// - The side-file names are fixed lower-case strings. Windows file lookup
///   ignores case. A port to a case-sensitive file system would find only
///   files named exactly so, unless its file layer folds case.
/// - The functions are plain string code with no platform calls, and they
///   do not touch game-logic state.
///
/// \ref sub_common_services covers the file system and strings, and
/// \ref sub_network the lobby and the game start.

/// \file Common/GetBasePathFromPath.cpp
/// \ingroup grp_w2_map_file_paths
/// \brief The map-folder name helpers: four path-splitting functions and
///        the eight functions that name a map's side files.
///
/// The file is named after its first function. Zero Hour keeps ten of
/// them, all but GetArtPreviewFromMap and GetPicPreviewFromMap, in
/// GameNetwork/FileTransfer.cpp, next to its map-transfer routine. In
/// BFME 2 retail all twelve sit together, directly before the
/// map-transfer routine.

/// \fn AsciiString GetBasePathFromPath(AsciiString path)
/// \brief Returns the folder part of a path: everything before the last
///        backslash.
///
/// This is the folder that every map side file lives in. The five
/// fixed-name helpers append a fixed file name to it, and the three
/// preview helpers append a name made from the `.map` file's base name.
/// Those eight are its only known callers.
///
/// \par Implementation
/// StringBase::reverseFind finds the last `\`. The characters before it are
/// copied into a temporary string with getBufferForRead and memcpy, and the
/// result is copied from that. The separator is dropped, so the folder has
/// no trailing backslash. With no backslash, the result is
/// AsciiString::TheEmptyString.
///
/// \par Retail quirk
/// A path with no backslash, such as a bare `MyMap.map`, has no folder, so
/// the side-file helpers then return a name that starts with a backslash,
/// such as `\map.ini`, rather than a name in the current folder.
///
/// \note Zero Hour asks getBufferForRead for one character more than the
///       folder's length. BFME 1 and BFME 2 ask for exactly the length:
///       BFME 2's StringBase getBufferForRead makes that the string's
///       length and reserves room for the terminator itself. The text
///       returned is the same.
///
/// \param path A file path that uses backslashes between folders.
/// \return The folder, without a trailing backslash, or the empty string
///         when path contains no backslash.
/// \see GetFileFromPath, GetBaseFileFromFile

/// \fn AsciiString GetFileFromPath(AsciiString path)
/// \brief Returns the file-name part of a path: everything after the last
///        backslash.
///
/// The three preview helpers use it to find the `.map` file's name before
/// stripping its extension with GetBaseFileFromFile. Those three are its
/// only known callers.
///
/// \par Implementation
/// StringBase::reverseFind finds the last `\`, and a new string is built
/// from the character after it. Unlike GetBasePathFromPath, a path with no
/// backslash is treated as all file name: the input is returned unchanged.
/// A path that ends in a backslash gives the empty string.
///
/// \param path A file path that uses backslashes between folders.
/// \return The text after the last backslash, or path itself when it
///         contains none.
/// \see GetBasePathFromPath, GetBaseFileFromFile

/// \fn AsciiString GetExtensionFromFile(AsciiString fname)
/// \brief Returns the extension of a file name: the text after its last
///        dot, without the dot.
///
/// The extension-side counterpart of GetBaseFileFromFile. No direct caller
/// in BFME 2's retail code is known, and Zero Hour defines it without
/// using it.
///
/// \par Implementation
/// StringBase::reverseFind finds the last `.`, and a new string is built
/// from the character after it. A name with no dot is returned unchanged,
/// not as an empty string.
///
/// \warning The search covers the whole string, folders included. Pass a
///          bare file name, for example from GetFileFromPath: given
///          `Maps\v1.2\MyMap`, the result is `2\MyMap`.
///
/// \param fname A file name, ideally without folders.
/// \return The text after the last dot, or fname itself when it contains
///         no dot.
/// \see GetBaseFileFromFile, GetFileFromPath

/// \fn AsciiString GetBaseFileFromFile(AsciiString fname)
/// \brief Returns a file name without its extension: everything before the
///        last dot.
///
/// The three preview helpers apply it to the result of GetFileFromPath, so
/// that `MyMap.map` gives the `MyMap` that each preview name starts with.
/// The retail preview helpers call it directly.
///
/// \par Implementation
/// The same steps as GetBasePathFromPath, searching for `.` instead of
/// `\`: the characters before the last dot are copied into a new string.
/// With no dot, the result is AsciiString::TheEmptyString, not the input.
///
/// \par Retail quirk
/// A `.map` file name with no extension therefore has an empty base name,
/// and the preview helpers return names such as `Maps\MyMap\.tga`.
///
/// \warning The search covers the whole string, folders included. Given
///          `Maps\v1.2\MyMap`, the result is `Maps\v1`. The preview helpers
///          avoid this by passing only the file name.
///
/// \param fname A file name, ideally without folders.
/// \return fname up to its last dot, or the empty string when it contains
///         no dot.
/// \see GetExtensionFromFile, GetFileFromPath, GetBasePathFromPath

/// \fn AsciiString GetPreviewFromMap(AsciiString path)
/// \brief Returns the name of a map's preview image: the map's folder, then
///        the `.map` file's base name with `.tga` added.
///
/// In retail it is the first of these helpers the map-transfer routine
/// calls (BFME 1: the first side file sent). GameInfo::setMap does not
/// call it. When the host looks for the preview, setMap removes the last
/// three characters of the map path and appends `tga`. That names the
/// same file only while the map's extension is three characters long.
///
/// \par Implementation
/// GetBaseFileFromFile of GetFileFromPath gives the base name, and
/// GetBasePathFromPath gives the folder. The two are joined with
/// AsciiString::format as folder, backslash, base name and `.tga`. Zero
/// Hour has the same body.
///
/// \param path The `.map` file's path, with backslashes between folders.
/// \return For `Maps\MyMap\MyMap.map`, `Maps\MyMap\MyMap.tga`.
/// \see GetArtPreviewFromMap, GetPicPreviewFromMap, GameInfo::setMap

/// \fn AsciiString GetArtPreviewFromMap(AsciiString path)
/// \brief Returns the name of a map's art preview: the map's folder, then
///        the `.map` file's base name with `_art.tga` added.
///
/// GameInfo::setMap uses it to look for the file on the host and sets
/// contents bit 128 when it is found. In retail the map-transfer routine
/// calls it (BFME 1: to send the file when its contents bit is set). The
/// art image is also read elsewhere, without this helper:
/// getMapPreviewImage prefers it to the plain preview, and
/// W3DRadar::buildTerrainTexture apparently uses it for the radar when
/// one is present.
///
/// \par Implementation
/// The same as GetPreviewFromMap, with `_art.tga` as the suffix.
///
/// \note Not in Zero Hour. BFME 1 has the same function.
///
/// \param path The `.map` file's path, with backslashes between folders.
/// \return For `Maps\MyMap\MyMap.map`, `Maps\MyMap\MyMap_art.tga`.
/// \see GetPreviewFromMap, GetPicPreviewFromMap, GameInfo::setMap

/// \fn AsciiString GetPicPreviewFromMap(AsciiString path)
/// \brief Returns the name of a map's picture preview: the map's folder,
///        then the `.map` file's base name with `_pic.tga` added.
///
/// GameInfo::setMap uses it to look for the file on the host and sets
/// contents bit 256 when it is found. In retail the map-transfer routine
/// calls it last of the side-file helpers (BFME 1: to send the file when
/// its contents bit is set).
///
/// \par Implementation
/// The same as GetPreviewFromMap, with `_pic.tga` as the suffix.
///
/// \note Not in Zero Hour. BFME 1 has the same function.
///
/// \param path The `.map` file's path, with backslashes between folders.
/// \return For `Maps\MyMap\MyMap.map`, `Maps\MyMap\MyMap_pic.tga`.
/// \see GetPreviewFromMap, GetArtPreviewFromMap, GameInfo::setMap

/// \fn AsciiString GetINIFromMap(AsciiString path)
/// \brief Returns the name of a map's INI override file, `map.ini`, in the
///        map's folder.
///
/// `map.ini` holds INI definitions that apply to this map only. In retail
/// the map-transfer routine calls it (BFME 1: to send the file when its
/// contents bit is set). GameInfo::setMap does not call it. To look for
/// the file, setMap joins the map path's folders with forward slashes and
/// appends `/map.ini`, as Zero Hour does.
///
/// \par Implementation
/// GetBasePathFromPath, then AsciiString::format with a backslash and
/// `map.ini`. The name does not depend on the map's own name. Zero Hour
/// has the same body.
///
/// \param path The `.map` file's path, with backslashes between folders.
/// \return For `Maps\MyMap\MyMap.map`, `Maps\MyMap\map.ini`.
/// \see GetSoloINIFromMap, GetStrFileFromMap, GetBasePathFromPath

/// \fn AsciiString GetSoloINIFromMap(AsciiString path)
/// \brief Returns the name of a map's `solo.ini` file in the map's folder.
///
/// The map loader reads `solo.ini`, like `map.ini`, as an INI override for
/// this map (\ref page_modding_ini). GameInfo::setMap uses this name to look
/// for the file on the host and sets contents bit 16 when it is found. In
/// retail the map-transfer routine calls it (BFME 1: to send the file when
/// its contents bit is set).
///
/// \par Implementation
/// GetBasePathFromPath, then a backslash and `solo.ini`. Zero Hour has the
/// same body.
///
/// \param path The `.map` file's path, with backslashes between folders.
/// \return For `Maps\MyMap\MyMap.map`, `Maps\MyMap\solo.ini`.
/// \see GetINIFromMap, GameInfo::setMap

/// \fn AsciiString GetStrFileFromMap(AsciiString path)
/// \brief Returns the name of a map's string file, `map.str`, in the map's
///        folder.
///
/// `map.str` holds the map's own strings, which the map loader reads when
/// the map loads (\ref page_modding_ini). GameInfo::setMap uses this name to
/// look for the file on the host and sets contents bit 8 when it is found.
/// In retail the map-transfer routine calls it (BFME 1: to send the file
/// when its contents bit is set).
///
/// \par Implementation
/// GetBasePathFromPath, then a backslash and `map.str`. Zero Hour has the
/// same body.
///
/// \param path The `.map` file's path, with backslashes between folders.
/// \return For `Maps\MyMap\MyMap.map`, `Maps\MyMap\map.str`.
/// \see GetINIFromMap, GameInfo::setMap

/// \fn AsciiString GetReadmeFromMap(AsciiString path)
/// \brief Returns the name of a map's `readme.txt` in the map's folder.
///
/// GameInfo::setMap uses it to look for the file on the host and sets
/// contents bit 64 when it is found. In retail the map-transfer routine
/// calls it (BFME 1: to send the file when its contents bit is set).
/// Zero Hour only looks for the file and transfers it; nothing else in
/// its source opens it. Retail BFME 2 holds no other string naming the
/// file, and no BFME 2 reader of it is established.
///
/// \par Implementation
/// GetBasePathFromPath, then a backslash and `readme.txt`. Zero Hour has
/// the same body.
///
/// \param path The `.map` file's path, with backslashes between folders.
/// \return For `Maps\MyMap\MyMap.map`, `Maps\MyMap\readme.txt`.
/// \see GetAssetUsageFromMap, GameInfo::setMap

/// \fn AsciiString GetAssetUsageFromMap(AsciiString path)
/// \brief Returns the name of a map's `assetusage.txt` in the map's
///        folder.
///
/// GameInfo::setMap uses it to look for the file on the host and sets
/// contents bit 32 when it is found. In retail the map-transfer routine
/// calls it (BFME 1: to send the file when its contents bit is set).
///
/// Zero Hour: the map loader, which reads `map.ini`, `solo.ini` and
/// `map.str`, also passes the folder's `AssetUsage.txt` (the same file on
/// a case-insensitive file system) to the display's asset purge. The
/// purge frees the loaded W3D assets that the file does not name,
/// skipping any word that starts with `;` as a comment. The BFME 1
/// source does the same. BFME 2's map loader reads the other three files
/// but has no such step, and retail BFME 2 holds no other string naming
/// the file, so no BFME 2 reader of it is established.
///
/// \par Implementation
/// GetBasePathFromPath, then a backslash and `assetusage.txt`. Zero Hour
/// has the same body.
///
/// \param path The `.map` file's path, with backslashes between folders.
/// \return For `Maps\MyMap\MyMap.map`, `Maps\MyMap\assetusage.txt`.
/// \see GetReadmeFromMap, GameInfo::setMap
